# netsurf: the stylesheet census -- nodeless batches split by the sheets that marked them (patch 316)
# Generated 2026-10-25
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 315)
#
# Doc 23 stage 1, census only (instrumentation; no reconvert changes).
# A sheet change reaches the reconvert as a mark that names no node
# (macos9_js_mark_dom_dirty, MACOS9_DOMMUT_UNKNOWN): the batch goes
# coarse with cause "nonode" and takes the full reconvert, and nothing
# records which sheet changed. Doc 23's stage 2 (anchored reach, local
# rebuild) only pays for single-sheet batches, and its open question 2
# asks how common multi-sheet windows are -- this patch measures that.
#
#  - html.h: struct html_stylesheet gains census_marks / census_closed
#    (both set to 0 at the two append sites; the initial array is
#    calloc'd).
#  - css.c: each of its two sheet-mark sites (a sheet finishing after
#    layout, html_convert_css_callback; and patch 266's mid-rebuild
#    deferral, noted when it is scheduled) attributes the mark to the
#    finishing entry (census_marks++). html_css_census_batch_sheets(c)
#    returns how many entries marked since the previous call and closes
#    them.
#  - macos9_reconvert.c: when a coarse batch commits its full reconvert
#    (macos9_reconvert_fullcause_count), it consumes the attribution;
#    for cause=nonode it logs "LIFE SHEETCAUSE sheets=N" synchronously
#    beside BATCHCAUSE and counts single (N=1) / multi (N>1) /
#    unidentified (N=0: a nodeless mark from a non-sheet caller). The
#    navigation reset prints "LIFE SHEETCENSUS single= multi=
#    unidentified=" on its own line, so the FULLCAUSE format the gate
#    matches is unchanged. An "over" batch consumes and discards its
#    attribution so it cannot leak into the next batch.
#
# Deviation from doc 23 piece A, recorded: identity is NOT carried on
# the mark (no macos9_js_mark_dom_dirty_sheet variant, no per-entry
# modification counter on html_css_process_modified_style). The census
# needs only batch-level attribution, which the entry counters give
# without touching the mark path; the payload-carrying variant belongs
# with stage 2, which is the first stage that would read it.
#
# First reading (focused, sim, JS-sheet-census): one <style> edited ->
# a nonode batch with sheets=1; two <style>s edited in one task -> one
# batch with sheets=2 (the two sheets' DONEs land in the same debounce
# window). Also visible: each edit costs TWO full reconverts -- the
# task's own mark on the <style> text node is a precise mark the local
# path declines (cause=local, then cause=two), and the sheet's nodeless
# batch follows. Stage 2 would have to answer both, not only the sheet
# batch; recorded for doc 23.
#
# Gate: JS-sheet-census (SHEETCENSUS 2/2 restyle checks) and its
# window's SHEETCAUSE lines: sheets=1 >= 1 and sheets>=2 >= 1.
#
# Simulator only; the vita cross-build was not run for this patch.
